    "narrative": "With the Zurich Zebras pushing for category gains in a tight 5x5 race, our lineup today centers around **Junior Caminero**, who earns an elite score of 72.77. Facing Shawn Armstrong, **Junior Caminero** occupies the optimal #3 spot, benefiting from a soft 4.35 xERA matchup that allows him to maximize his power-speed profile. While other depth pieces like **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Colt Keith** are prepared to rotate in, **Junior Caminero** remains our primary anchor. We are keeping a close eye on the official confirmation of the batting order; should **Junior Caminero** drop out of the top three, we will recalibrate his expected efficiency, though his current platoon advantage against the right-handed Armstrong provides enough of a cushion to maintain his status as a must-start.\n\nThe bench remains heavy today due to off-days for our core contributors **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Christian Yelich**. Among those active but relegated to the pine, **Lars Nootbaar** and **Josh Smith** were the final cuts. While **Lars Nootbaar** offers a high OBP floor, he lacked the aggressive upside against his projected starter, whereas **Josh Smith** was squeezed out due to his current situational volatility. We are carefully monitoring the status of **Gary Sanchez** and **Dillon Dingler** behind the plate; if the weather in the Northeast creates a delay risk for their contest, we will pivot to **Casey Schmitt** to ensure we maintain our game-cap efficiency. The rest of the taxi squad\u2014including **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Carson Benge**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014are held in reserve for injury contingencies or potential late-inning pinch-hit opportunities to bolster our stolen base totals.",
